  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nSetups that aren't configured yet no longer hide configured ones (#383, closes #381). A method setup took part in matching as soon as its arguments were given, before Returns, Throws or Callback configured it. Until then, a matching call returned the default value or threw MissingImposterException, even when an older setup had an outcome. That could happen in three ways:\n\nanother thread called while a setup was being added;\n\nverifying with narrower arguments created a setup, as in imposter.Get(Arg\\<int>.Is(5)).Called(Count.Once()), which made later Get(5) calls lose an earlier Returns;\n\na call went through a setup before its first outcome was configured, and that configuration was then lost.\n\nA call now uses the newest matching setup that has an outcome. A setup without one is used only when nothing configured matches, so a bare void setup still allows its call in explicit mode. Behaviour change: a newer bare setup no longer overrides an older Throws or Callback for the same arguments. To make such a case do nothing, give its setup an empty callback: .Callback(\\_ => { }).\n\nMaintenance\n\nDebug builds of the generator no longer warn about an unused using (#385, closes #384). No behaviour change.",
